.el .ds Aq '
.TH PDFLUENT-PROTECT 1  "pdfluent 1.1.0" PDFluent
.SH NAME
pdfluent\-protect \- Set a password and restrict permissions
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpdfluent protect\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] <\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-out\fR> [\fB\-\-password\-file\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-owner\-password\-file\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-algorithm\fR] [\fB\-\-permissions\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set a password and restrict permissions
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON envelope on stdout
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Output PDF, or `\-` for stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Password file: line 1 is the user password, line 2 (if present) the owner password. Without it, PDFLUENT_PASSWORD and PDFLUENT_OWNER_PASSWORD, then an interactive prompt
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Quiet: human mode prints data only (no warnings or progress notes)
.TP
\fB\-\-owner\-password\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Owner\-password file (line 1). Overrides line 2 of \-\-password\-file
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose stderr diagnostics (repeat for more)
.TP
\fB\-\-algorithm\fR \fI<ALGORITHM>\fR [default: aes256]
Encryption algorithm
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
aes256: AES\-256 (default)
.IP \(bu 2
aes128: AES\-128, for readers older than PDF 1.7 ext
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-permissions\fR \fI<PERMISSIONS>\fR [default: full]
Reader permissions
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
full: Authorised readers may do anything
.IP \(bu 2
print\-only: Printing only
.IP \(bu 2
read\-only: Reading only
.IP \(bu 2
annotate: Reading plus annotation
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite the existing output file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
Input PDF, or `\-` for stdin
.SH VERSION
v1.1.0
